;; Frames and threads (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.4; PYS7 (a)): a frame is a heap object holding a code
;; object's locals, cells, value stack and instruction index; the dispatch loop (eval.go) runs a
;; thread's frames without holding them on Go's stack, so a call from Python to Python is a new frame
;; and a return pops it, and a generator (PY5d) is a frame kept between resumptions.


